A simple way to track gym progress without a coach is to log every session with the same exercise names, then review weekly volume, completed sessions, and personal bests. Memory inflates PRs and hides missed weeks. A structured workout log makes the trend visible in minutes.

## What to record

- Date and session type (strength, cardio, yoga, Pilates, stretching)
- The same exercise names week to week
- Sets, reps, and load
- Optional rest and one short note

## A weekly review that actually works

1. Count how many planned sessions you logged.
1. Compare volume on two or three main lifts versus last week.
1. Note any new personal bests.
1. Decide: keep the load, add a little, or deload.
1. Save that as next week’s template so you do not rebuild the session from scratch.

## What not to use as proof

- How hard it felt
- A random PR on a lift you never logged before
- Screenshots with no dates or sets

PushLab is built for this loop: log in the gym (offline if needed), then check volume, consistency, and PRs in one place. It is not a medical device and does not read Apple Health.
